description:
A DLL exports by ordinal, so a new version must keep every published ordinal. Write

```cpp
std::vector<std::string> ordinalProblems(const std::map<std::string, int>& oldVersion, const std::map<std::string, int>& newVersion);
```

Each map is export name to ordinal. Report, in this order:

1. for each name in the old version (in alphabetical order, as the map stores them):
   - missing from the new version: `"<name> was removed"`;
   - present with a different ordinal: `"<name> moved from @<old> to @<new>"`;
2. then, for each name that is **new** (alphabetical): if its ordinal was used by a different name in the old version, `"@<n> now means <newName>, was <oldName>"`.

An empty list means old programs keep working.

```
old: { stackHeight: 1, stackWeight: 2, debugDump: 3 }
new: { stackHeight: 1, stackWeight: 5, layers: 3 }
problems: "debugDump was removed", "stackWeight moved from @2 to @5", "@3 now means layers, was debugDump"
```

